## Phase 1 — Storage and data layer (SQL)
- SQLAlchemy with SQLite by default, Postgres-ready via config.
- Tables: `instruments`, `timeseries` (long format: ticker, field, date, value, source,
  fetched_at), `events` (type, datetime, actual, consensus/expectation, prior),
  `opec_meetings`, `geopolitical_events`, `positions`, `fundamentals` (reference date
  AND publication date), `fetch_log`.
- Incremental fetches only; batch requests; log request counts (Bloomberg data limits).
- Store publication dates so analytics never use data early (EIA weekly data releases
  Wednesday for the prior week; CFTC is as of Tuesday, released Friday; IEA/OPEC/EIA
  monthly reports publish with lags and get revised — store vintages where possible).
- Session alignment: ICE Brent, NYMEX WTI, Singapore products and FX closes differ.
  Make snapshot time configurable and document the choice.
- Ticker verification report: every configured ticker and field is tested; failures
  and sparse series are listed, never silently skipped.

